('Proxy vs Decorator','Dynamic Proxy differs from Decorator in that:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Inheritance','["Decorator only works on interfaces","Dynamic Proxy is created at runtime via reflection; Decorator is a compile-time wrapper","They are identical","Decorator requires inheritance"]','Dynamic Proxy is created at runtime via reflection; Decorator is a compile-time wrapper'),
('Open Closed','The Open/Closed Principle states:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Inheritance','["Classes must be open for modification","Classes should be open for extension but closed for modification","Interfaces should be closed","Methods must be final"]','Classes should be open for extension but closed for modification'),
('Functional Interface','A functional interface has exactly:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Inheritance','["No methods","One abstract method","Two methods","Only default methods"]','One abstract method'),
('Interface Segregation','The Interface Segregation Principle states:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Inheritance','["One interface per project","Clients should not be forced to depend on methods they do not use","Interfaces should be large","Only abstract classes, no interfaces"]','Clients should not be forced to depend on methods they do not use'),
('Widening Narrowing','Widening reference conversion is:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Inheritance','["Downcasting","Upcasting (subtype to supertype) — always implicit and safe","Casting primitive to object","Always requires explicit cast"]','Upcasting (subtype to supertype) — always implicit and safe'),
