('Bool Getter','Write a public getter named isActive for a private boolean field active.','CODING','EASY','OOP','Encapsulation',NULL,'public boolean isActive() { return active; }'),
('Validated Setter','Write a setter for private int age that only assigns if age >= 0.','CODING','EASY','OOP','Encapsulation',NULL,'public void setAge(int age) { if(age >= 0) this.age = age; }'),

-- ================================================================
--  OOP / ENCAPSULATION  —  MEDIUM
-- ================================================================
('Defensive Copy','Returning a mutable Date field from a getter should return:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["The original reference","A new Date with the same time value (defensive copy)","null","A string version"]','A new Date with the same time value (defensive copy)'),
('Law of Demeter','The Law of Demeter states a method should only call methods on:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Any object in the system","Its own object, parameters, fields, and locally created objects","Only static methods","Only objects passed via constructor"]','Its own object, parameters, fields, and locally created objects'),
('Tell Dont Ask','Tell, Don''t Ask principle means:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Tell the compiler the type","Ask objects for data, then decide for them","Tell objects what to do rather than asking for data to make decisions externally","Ask for permissions before calling methods"]','Tell objects what to do rather than asking for data to make decisions externally'),
('Package Private Use','Package-private classes are useful for:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Public APIs","Helper classes not part of a package''s public API","Global utilities","Abstract base classes"]','Helper classes not part of a package''s public API'),
('Record Encap','Java Records provide encapsulation by:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Making fields public mutable","Making fields private final with auto-generated accessors, equals, hashCode","Allowing arbitrary setters","Using reflection"]','Making fields private final with auto-generated accessors, equals, hashCode'),
('Sync Encap','Encapsulating mutable shared state with synchronized methods:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Slows down programs always","Hides thread-safety complexity from callers","Requires callers to synchronize manually","Prevents GC"]','Hides thread-safety complexity from callers'),
('Immutable Deep','A truly immutable class must:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Have no methods","Make a defensive copy of mutable objects passed in and returned","Use volatile fields","Have only static methods"]','Make a defensive copy of mutable objects passed in and returned'),
('Module JPMS','Java 9 modules (module-info.java) extend encapsulation by:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Making all classes private","Restricting which packages are exported and accessible outside the module","Adding new access modifiers","Preventing reflection always"]','Restricting which packages are exported and accessible outside the module'),
('Builder Encap','The Builder pattern encapsulates:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Execution logic","Object construction complexity and validates the object before building","Database queries","UI rendering"]','Object construction complexity and validates the object before building'),
('Encap Interface','Programming to an interface promotes encapsulation because:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Interfaces have no fields","Callers depend on the interface, not the concrete implementation — internals can change freely","Interfaces are immutable","Interfaces prevent subclassing"]','Callers depend on the interface, not the concrete implementation — internals can change freely'),
('Coupling','High coupling between classes means:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Good encapsulation","Classes are highly dependent on each other''s internal details — bad for maintainability","Better performance","Easier testing"]','Classes are highly dependent on each other''s internal details — bad for maintainability'),
('Copy Constructor Encap','A copy constructor in a mutable class ensures:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["The copy shares the same mutable reference","The copy is a deep copy, preventing aliasing bugs","The copy is a shallow copy","The original cannot change"]','The copy is a deep copy, preventing aliasing bugs'),
('Cohesion','High cohesion means:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["A class has many responsibilities","A class has a single, well-defined responsibility — strong encapsulation","Methods are long","Classes are coupled"]','A class has a single, well-defined responsibility — strong encapsulation'),
('Mutable Param','When a constructor receives a mutable List, proper encapsulation requires:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Storing the reference directly","Making a copy of the list and storing the copy","Converting to an array","Making the field public"]','Making a copy of the list and storing the copy'),
('Private Const','Having a private constructor in a class means:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["No objects can be created","The class cannot be extended, and instantiation is controlled (e.g. Singleton, factory)","All methods must be static","The class is abstract"]','The class cannot be extended, and instantiation is controlled (e.g. Singleton, factory)'),
('Static Field Encap','A mutable public static field breaks encapsulation because:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Static fields are slow","Any class can modify it directly, bypassing any validation logic","Static fields cannot be final","Only one class can use it"]','Any class can modify it directly, bypassing any validation logic'),
('Accessor in Record','Accessing a field in a Java Record uses:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Getter via get prefix (getName())","Direct field access","Accessor method with same name as field (name())","Static method"]','Accessor method with same name as field (name())'),
('DTOvsEntity','DTO (Data Transfer Object) promotes encapsulation by:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Replacing all entities","Exposing only the data needed for a specific use case, hiding entity internals","Making all fields public","Using inheritance from Entity"]','Exposing only the data needed for a specific use case, hiding entity internals'),
('Encap Testing','Encapsulation can hinder unit testing because:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Private fields are untestable in principle","Private methods can only be tested indirectly through public APIs (which is actually preferred)","Getters are slower","Tests require reflection always"]','Private methods can only be tested indirectly through public APIs (which is actually preferred)'),
('Opaque Type','An opaque type hides its implementation by:','MCQ','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation','["Using primitives","Exposing only an interface/abstract type to callers, hiding the concrete class","Making the class final","Using generics"]','Exposing only an interface/abstract type to callers, hiding the concrete class'),
-- MEDIUM CODING
('Defensive Copy Code','Write a getter for a private Date field birthDate that returns a defensive copy.','CODING','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation',NULL,'public Date getBirthDate() { return new Date(birthDate.getTime()); }'),
('Immutable List Return','Write a getter for a private List<String> items that returns an unmodifiable view.','CODING','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation',NULL,'public List<String> getItems() { return Collections.unmodifiableList(items); }'),
('Private Constructor','Write a private constructor for class Singleton with no body.','CODING','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation',NULL,'private Singleton() {}'),
('Validate Age','Write a setter for int field age that throws IllegalArgumentException if age is negative.','CODING','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation',NULL,'public void setAge(int age) { if(age < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Age cannot be negative"); this.age = age; }'),
('Final Field Init','Write a constructor for class Point that initializes two final int fields x and y.','CODING','MEDIUM','OOP','Encapsulation',NULL,'public Point(int x, int y) { this.x = x; this.y = y; }'),

