('JPMS Exports','In Java 9 module-info.java, exports com.example means:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["All packages are exported","Only com.example package is accessible to other modules","All public types in com.example become private","Nothing — exports are automatic"]','Only com.example package is accessible to other modules'),
('Encap Concurrency','Which class provides the best encapsulation of thread-safe mutable state?','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["A class with public fields + external synchronization","A class with private fields + internally synchronized methods","A class with volatile fields","A class with final fields"]','A class with private fields + internally synchronized methods'),
('Value Object','A Value Object (DDD term) is characterized by:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Having a mutable identity","Being immutable and defined by its attribute values, not identity","Having a database ID","Extending Entity"]','Being immutable and defined by its attribute values, not identity'),
('Encap Reflection','Java reflection can bypass encapsulation using:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Only public APIs","field.setAccessible(true) — then private fields can be read/written","Proxy classes","Static methods only"]','field.setAccessible(true) — then private fields can be read/written'),
('Deep Immutability','Deep immutability requires:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Only final fields","All referenced mutable objects to also be made immutable or defensively copied","Private setters","A record type"]','All referenced mutable objects to also be made immutable or defensively copied'),
('LoD Violation','a.getB().getC().doSomething() violates the Law of Demeter because:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["It has too many method calls","It traverses the object graph, coupling a to the internal structure of B and C","It breaks polymorphism","Methods should not return objects"]','It traverses the object graph, coupling a to the internal structure of B and C'),
('Module Qualified Exports','Qualified exports (exports com.pkg to other.module) in Java 9:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Exports to all","Export only to specified modules — fine-grained encapsulation","Are deprecated","Require reflection"]','Export only to specified modules — fine-grained encapsulation'),
('Persistent Immutable','When building immutable collections that support efficient functional updates, Java uses:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["ArrayList copy","Structural sharing (persistent data structures) — sharing unmodified parts","Always copying the full collection","Arrays instead"]','Structural sharing (persistent data structures) — sharing unmodified parts'),
('sealed Encap','Sealed classes contribute to encapsulation by:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Making classes abstract","Restricting which classes can extend a type, preventing unexpected external subclassing","Making all fields private","Preventing reflection"]','Restricting which classes can extend a type, preventing unexpected external subclassing'),
('SOLID SRP','Single Responsibility Principle and encapsulation relate because:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["They are unrelated","A class with one responsibility has a tighter, better-encapsulated boundary","SRP requires many classes","Encapsulation implies multiple responsibilities"]','A class with one responsibility has a tighter, better-encapsulated boundary'),
('Encap AOP','Aspect-Oriented Programming (AOP) can break encapsulation by:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Adding methods","Weaving cross-cutting concerns into private implementation details at bytecode level","Removing methods","Adding interfaces"]','Weaving cross-cutting concerns into private implementation details at bytecode level'),
('Stack Encap','A Stack ADT encapsulates its internal array by:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Exposing the array directly","Hiding the array and exposing only push, pop, peek, and isEmpty","Making the array public final","Using generics only"]','Hiding the array and exposing only push, pop, peek, and isEmpty'),
('open Module','In Java 9, open module opens ALL packages to reflection. This is less encapsulated than a normal module because:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["It is faster","Runtime reflection can access all packages, even non-exported ones","It restricts more","It has no effect"]','Runtime reflection can access all packages, even non-exported ones'),
('Abstract Type','Using abstract types (interfaces/abstract classes) in public APIs promotes encapsulation because:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Abstract classes are faster","Concrete implementation details are hidden behind the abstraction boundary","It prevents polymorphism","It removes the need for tests"]','Concrete implementation details are hidden behind the abstraction boundary'),
('Encap Inheritance Break','Why does inheritance break encapsulation?','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["It is always fine","Subclasses depend on parent internals; changes to parent can break subclasses","Inheritance removes access modifiers","Inheritance duplicates code"]','Subclasses depend on parent internals; changes to parent can break subclasses'),
('Composition Encap','Composition is preferred over inheritance for encapsulation because:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Composition is faster","The composed object''s internals are fully hidden; the outer class is not affected by changes to the inner class","Composition allows multiple inheritance","Composition reduces code"]','The composed object''s internals are fully hidden; the outer class is not affected by changes to the inner class'),
('Visibility Grid','A member with protected access in class A can be accessed from:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Anywhere","Only in A","A, same package, and subclasses of A (in any package)","A and subclasses only (not same package others)"]','A, same package, and subclasses of A (in any package)'),
('Encap by Contract','Design by Contract (pre/postconditions, invariants) relates to encapsulation by:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Replacing access modifiers","Formally specifying what a class guarantees, strengthening the encapsulation boundary with verifiable rules","Removing getters","Requiring public fields"]','Formally specifying what a class guarantees, strengthening the encapsulation boundary with verifiable rules'),
('Visiblity Subclass','A subclass in a different package can access a parent''s protected member:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Always","Only through a reference of the subclass type or its subtype, not through a parent-type reference","Never","Only if the member is also static"]','Only through a reference of the subclass type or its subtype, not through a parent-type reference'),
('Encap Final','Making a class final ensures encapsulation by:','MCQ','HARD','OOP','Encapsulation','["Removing all methods","Preventing subclasses from modifying or overriding the encapsulated behavior","Making fields private","Adding synchronization"]','Preventing subclasses from modifying or overriding the encapsulated behavior'),
